@@ -3,3 +3,14 @@
 A small TypeScript library, with no runtime dependency, of building blocks for our services that store,
 exchange and update JSON: configuration files, API payloads and stored records. It is imported by the
 other projects of the team, so its behaviour must follow the published standards it implements.
+
+## API
+
+### `resolvePointer(document, pointer)`
+
+Implements JSON Pointer (RFC 6901). Returns the value `pointer` refers to in `document`; the empty
+pointer returns the whole document. Throws `JsonPointerError` if the pointer is syntactically invalid
+(section 3), or does not resolve to a value: missing member, array index out of range or not in
+canonical form, the `-` token (section 4: nonexistent element), or traversal into a primitive. Only
+own members are looked up, so `__proto__`, `constructor` etc. never resolve to inherited values.
+The document is never modified.
